From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: the desk profile's fps caps the stream

Moonlight offers the client display's rate: a 180 Hz laptop streamed a
desk at 180 fps while the desk profile (and the game FPS limits the
service sets from it) said 144. The encoder, the composition rate (Auto
follows the fastest stream) and the Wi-Fi link carried a quarter more
frames, mostly repeats.

The Profile's `fps` (sent with every welcome and set_profile) now caps
the frame rate of the next stream: RTSP takes min(client's maxFPS,
profile fps) and drops the client's display rate (framerateX100), which
no longer matches. The stream object reports the capped rate as
fps_requested and what the client asked for as fps_client (null when
not capped). A profile without fps keeps the client's rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J21Rm5JX5ZLQfFmc8j2sUj

diff --git a/src/rtsp.cpp b/src/rtsp.cpp
index f413cbe372ac4f80d3c6502e63b5089efa7834d3..7da6cb3d784461af043b94c79747ce5bf821434f 100644
--- a/src/rtsp.cpp
+++ b/src/rtsp.cpp
@@ -1194,6 +1194,13 @@ namespace rtsp_stream {
           config.monitor.framerateX100 = 0;
         }
       }
+      // SplitPlay: the desk profile's fps caps the stream. The client's display rate (framerateX100) no longer matches.
+      if (const int sp_fps = splitplay::profile::stream_fps(config.monitor.framerate); sp_fps != config.monitor.framerate) {
+        BOOST_LOG(info) << "SplitPlay: the client asked for "sv << config.monitor.framerate << " fps, the desk profile streams at most "sv << sp_fps;
+        config.monitor.sp_fps_client = config.monitor.framerate;
+        config.monitor.framerate = sp_fps;
+        config.monitor.framerateX100 = 0;
+      }
       config.monitor.bitrate = (int) util::from_view(args.at("x-nv-vqos[0].bw.maximumBitrateKbps"sv));
       config.monitor.slicesPerFrame = (int) util::from_view(args.at("x-nv-video[0].videoEncoderSlicesPerFrame"sv));
       config.monitor.numRefFrames = (int) util::from_view(args.at("x-nv-video[0].maxNumReferenceFrames"sv));
